(b) To assist in organising and delivering training on promoting student mental health for teachers, parents and students;
(c) To assist in networking school teachers as resource persons for mental health promotion;
(d) To provide general and administrative support on coordinating of training and resources production;
(e) To provide psycho-educational assessment and intervention for students with learning, emotional and/or behavioural difficulties;
(f) To provide consultation and support to school personnel and parents for students with diverse educational needs; and
(g) To carry out ad hoc duties as assigned by supervisors.
Terms of Appointment: Successful candidates will be employed on non-civil service contract terms for 1 year.
